.TH HEAD 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
head \- output the first part of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B head
.RB [ \-n
.IR lines ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR bytes ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B head
writes the first 10 lines of each
.I file
to standard output.
With no
.IR file ,
or where a
.I file
is
.BR \- ,
it reads standard input.
.PP
With more than one
.IR file ,
each one's output is preceded by a header,
.BI "==> " name " <=="
(\fBstandard input\fR for \fB\-\fR), with a blank line between files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR \fIlines\fR, \fB\-n\fIlines\fR, \fB\-\fIlines\fR
Print the first
.I lines
lines instead of 10.
.B \-n
also turns off an earlier
.BR \-c .
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIbytes\fR, \fB\-c\fIbytes\fR
Print the first
.I bytes
bytes instead of lines.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if a file could not be opened or a number was invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
head \-n 3 /init.lua
ls \-1 | head \-5
.fi
.SH NOTES
Negative counts (GNU's "all but the last
.IR n ")
are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tail (1),
.BR cat (1),
.BR less (1)
